Board-move and outcome cues in this directory come from two places.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Board-move cues - Creative Commons Zero (CC0 1.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are built from the "Chess Puzzle Blitz SFX" pack by el_boss
(Jeff Final Boss), recorded on a wooden board and released CC0 1.0. Every
cue is pitched down to 0.78x and given a -3dB treble shelf, which is what
makes the set read as a heavy board rather than a light one:

  move.mp3    <- Piece Placement.mp3
  capture.mp3 <- Piece Capture.mp3
  castle.mp3  <- Piece Slide.mp3 + Piece Placement.mp3, layered 130ms apart
                 so the king slides and the rook is set down beside it
  check.mp3   <- Piece Placement.mp3 with a short ring, so the ring marks a
                 check rather than a higher pitch
  start.mp3   <- Board Start.mp3

  https://freesound.org/people/el_boss/packs/30764/

License: Creative Commons Zero, CC0 1.0 Universal
http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

CC0 waives attribution, so this file is a record of where the audio came
from rather than a condition of using it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Outcome cues - original, Apache License 2.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are synthesized mallet phrases written for KiriChess and are part of
the Apache-2.0 work. They carry the same pitch-down as the cues above so the
whole set sits in one register:

  win.mp3     a short rising phrase
  loss.mp3    a short falling phrase
  draw.mp3    a single neutral note
